# The permission lasts only while Nowhere to Run is on the battlefield. On turn five Bot1 casts it (the enters trigger kills
# Bot2's Elvish Mystic), then Lightning Bolt at Bot2's hexproof Sylvan Caryatid - a legal target while the enchantment is out.
# Bot2 responds with Disenchant on Nowhere to Run; it resolves first, and the Bolt's target is illegal on resolution
# (CR 608.2b, and the ruling: "that creature becomes an illegal target for that spell or ability"), so the Bolt does nothing and
# the Caryatid is undamaged. A second Bolt is then refused at the Caryatid, the way it would have been before the enchantment.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Nowhere to Run
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Swamp
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Sylvan Caryatid
Elvish Mystic
Disenchant
Plains
Island x12

